{
  "name": "Offshore water injection module",
  "description": "Water injection module on a 4-leg jacket. Seawater lift pump P-W300 feeds the multimedia filter package X-W330, which backwashes to dump caisson CS-W350; filtered water is deaerated in the packed vacuum deaerator T-W320, dosed with oxygen scavenger and antifoam from C-W340, with the overhead going to the vacuum package. Duty / standby booster pumps P-W305A/B feed duty / standby multistage injection pumps P-W310A/B, which discharge through check valves into an injection header that drops through a check valve and ESDV into each of the two jacket risers to the injection flowlines.",
  "source": "Deck Twin example (illustrative layout, not a real asset)",
